{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"alabaster-incapable-hare","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nThe A6-0b live deployment preflight and final receipt found two pre-existing untracked event JSONs in the persistent review-bot tickets clone while HEAD exactly equalled refs/remotes/origin/tickets:\n\n- 172e-b207-4c18-4243/1785522649620648380-d92b157f-3a3e-4c66-85d9-b5f2ec06499e-TICKET_DIGEST.json\n- 7ab3-9df0-7a90-4ffd/1785820923597137671-b00b8061-e68a-4ab1-8f13-0625c90da09e-CLAIM_ENRICH.json\n\nThey predate the A6-0b deployment. Ref convergence is healthy and there is no tracked diff, merge, rebase, or stash state, but a history rewrite/reset could overwrite or strand these uncommitted artifacts. Do not delete or raw-commit them without determining whether they are unique canonical events or duplicates.\n\n## Plan\n- Inspect only event identity/type/authorship metadata and compare each event UUID/path with the authoritative tickets branch.\n- Determine whether each artifact is unique recoverable data, a duplicate of a committed event, or disposable failed-write residue.\n- Recover unique events through the normal signed store write path, or record evidence supporting explicit deletion if duplicate/disposable.\n- Re-run clone integrity/ref-convergence checks and prove the persistent clone has no untracked event files before the A6-1 publication window.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] Each stranded path has a documented identity/duplication determination against authoritative origin/tickets.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] Any unique event is recovered through a normal signed store operation, or explicit operator evidence authorizes discarding a duplicate/disposable file.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] Persistent review-bot clone HEAD equals refs/remotes/origin/tickets with no tracked or untracked event files, merge, rebase, or stash state.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] The final clean-clone receipt is recorded before the A6-1 reclaim publication window.\n\nNo production source change is presumed; if investigation finds a reproducible writer defect, file a separate code bug with the reproduction.","id":"b626-65ee-df80-44dc","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":["reviewbot","tickets-store","reclaim"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Recover stranded review-bot event files before tickets reclaim"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785841860041543001,"uuid":"5f490d1f-56b0-46da-a147-979c04c7d920"}